1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,373
Do you know how to intrude

2
00:00:01,373 --> 00:00:02,595
the lower incisors without

3
00:00:02,595 --> 00:00:04,165
changing their inclination?

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,457
It all depends on where

5
00:00:05,457 --> 00:00:07,204
the line of action of the force passes

6
00:00:07,204 --> 00:00:09,205
relative to the center of resistance.

7
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,161
If the force passes in front of it,

8
00:00:17,161 --> 00:00:19,269
the incisors tend to tip labially.

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,359
If the line of action passes

10
00:00:27,359 --> 00:00:29,079
through the center of resistance,

11
00:00:29,079 --> 00:00:30,122
we get predominantly

12
00:00:30,122 --> 00:00:31,308
bodily intrusion.

13
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,500
But what happens if we shift

14
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,401
the line of action

15
00:00:35,401 --> 00:00:37,301
behind the center of resistance?

16
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,218
An opposite moment arises,

17
00:00:39,218 --> 00:00:40,629
promoting lingual tipping

18
00:00:40,629 --> 00:00:41,719
of the crowns.

19
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:46,854
One cantilever.

20
00:00:46,854 --> 00:00:48,108
Three lines of action.

21
00:00:48,108 --> 00:00:50,572
Three different biomechanical effects.

22
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,348
That's why it's important to control

23
00:00:53,348 --> 00:00:55,146
not only the magnitude of the force,

24
00:00:55,146 --> 00:00:56,795
but also its point of application

25
00:00:56,795 --> 00:00:57,794
and direction.
